        "comments": "The assembly daLatSqua1.hap1.1 is based on 127x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Based on evidence such as Khmer profiling (smudge plot) and BUSCO duplication rate, it is clear that this species is tetraploid. The HiC signal suggests that it is two highly divergent sub genomes of a historic allotetraploidy event.",
